.TH PI-CLOCK 1 "October 2026" "pi-clock" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pi-clock \- terminal clock that expresses local time as multiples of pi
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pi-clock
.RI [ tui ]
.br
.B pi-clock
.B --no-tray
.br
.B pi-clock
.B tray
.br
.B pi-clock
.B help
.br
.B pi-clock
.B version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pi-clock
shows local time in a terminal UI and, in tray-enabled builds, starts a system-tray clock alongside it. The dial is 12-hour; the numeric pi-time tracks the full 24-hour day.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --no-tray
Run only the terminal UI.
.TP
.B tray
Run only the system-tray app. Available when built with the tray-app feature.
.TP
.B help
Show command help.
.TP
.B version
Show the installed version.
.SH TUI KEYS
.TP
.B q, Esc
Exit the TUI.
.TP
.B c
Toggle color.
.TP
.B ?
Show or hide help.
.SH VERSION
The package version is maintained in Cargo.toml and published as matching vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH Git tags.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cargo (1)
